# Player gameplay rules

## Authority

- Commands: `PlayerGameplayBridge` → typed `PlayerActionRequest` → `PlayerGameplayService`
- Physical evidence: `PhysicalInteractionBridge` → `PhysicalOutcomePayload`
- Do not scatter sidecar calls from client screens

## Interaction sessions

`PlayerInteractionSessions` binds player + citizen + settlement + expiry/distance.
Subsequent UI choices reference the session. Max interact distance: 8 blocks.

## Typed actions only if handled

`PlayerActionType` enumerates only actions with real handlers. No unused catalogue.

## Reputation / standing

Single number: `PlayerReputationState`. UI attitude labels derive from standing/reputation/legal — no second fame system.
`FactionStanding`: NEUTRAL → CITIZEN → TRUSTED → OFFICIAL → RULER.

## Tasks

Lifecycle: OPEN → DISCOVERED → ACCEPTED → COMPLETED (also FAILED/ABANDONED/EXPIRED).
Completion requires server-verified evidence (inventory delivery, camp clear, caravan arrival).

## Trade

Buy/sell: NeoForge consumes/refunds items + gold, then canonical stockpile/market update.
Reject unverified (`serverVerified`) transactions.

## Crime / guards

Player offences create `CrimeState` with `playerOffender` + legal record.
Guards use cached wanted/hostile flags — never IPC inside AI predicates.

## Multi-world

Clear `FactionDispositionCache` and `PlayerInteractionSessions` on server stop with other session caches.
